  "html": "<h1>TreeView</h1>\n<p>Use <code>TreeView&lt;T&gt;</code> for navigation, document outlines and hierarchical pickers.\nIt is a standalone component built on <code>VirtualList</code>, not a one-column DataGrid.\nOnly visible rows are rendered; expanded items and loaded children remain in memory.</p>\n<h2 id=\"lazy-asynchronous-branches\">Lazy asynchronous branches</h2>\n<p>Expand <strong>Pages</strong> and <strong>Media</strong> to load their children. <strong>Retry example</strong> deliberately\nfails once: its inline Retry button reloads only that branch. The request counter\nalso demonstrates that collapsing and reopening a successful branch uses its cache.\nUse <strong>Show nested example</strong> to open Pages → Guides → Getting started → Tutorials.\nMixed folders and leaves across five levels demonstrate indentation and reserved\ndisclosure space; a long title also exercises single-line truncation.\nThe custom renderer adds open/closed folder icons and page/image icons without\nchanging the accessible labels or TreeView’s disclosure controls.</p>\n<div data-live-demo=\"tree-view-overview\"></div>\n<h2 id=\"data-adapter\">Data adapter</h2>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">const</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> tree</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> new</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> TreeView</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">FileItem</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">>({</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    label: </span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"Files\"</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">    getText</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">item</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> =></span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> item.name,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    data: {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">        getKey</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">item</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> =></span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> item.id,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">        hasChildren</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">item</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> =></span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> item.isFolder,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">        getChildren</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: (</span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">item</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">signal</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=></span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> loadChildren</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(item?.id, signal)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">});</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">tree.dom.style.height </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> \"300px\"</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">tree.</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">mount</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(container);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span></code></pre>\n<p><code>getChildren(undefined, signal)</code> requests roots. Every call returns <strong>all immediate\nchildren</strong>, either as an array or a Promise. Pagination is not part of this contract.\nKeys must be globally unique, stable strings, including across different parents.\n<code>hasChildren</code> must be available before loading a branch; a successfully loaded empty\nbranch loses its disclosure arrow.</p>\n<p>Loading and error rows belong to their branch and do not replace the rest of the\ntree. Concurrent requests for the same branch are shared. Collapsing retains both\ncached children and in-flight work; reopening does not start a duplicate request.</p>\n<h2 id=\"cache-and-lifetime\">Cache and lifetime</h2>\n<p>Mounting starts root loading. <code>load()</code> can also start it explicitly and shares the\nexisting request. <code>expand(item)</code> loads a known item’s children when needed;\n<code>collapse(item)</code> hides descendants without discarding them.</p>\n<p><code>await tree.refresh(item)</code> invalidates and reloads a branch’s descendants;\n<code>await tree.refresh()</code> reloads the whole tree. Stable keys retain expansion and\nselection when their items are loaded again. A missing selected item clears the\nselection after loading finishes. Refresh aborts invalidated requests. Dispose\naborts all requests, and late responses are ignored even if a loader ignores its signal.</p>\n<p>Loader failures are shown locally rather than rejected from <code>load</code>, <code>expand</code> or\n<code>refresh</code>. Do not use their Promise fulfillment as proof that a remote request succeeded.\nTreeView does not infer external data changes: call <code>refresh</code> when the adapter changes.</p>\n<h2 id=\"focus-selection-and-activation\">Focus, selection and activation</h2>\n<p>Focus and selection are independent. Arrow Up/Down and Home/End move focus;\nRight opens a branch or enters its first child, and Left collapses it or moves\nto its parent. Typing a label prefix finds a visible item. Space selects;\nEnter selects and activates. Clicking selects; double-clicking activates.</p>\n<p>Subscribe to <code>selectionChanged</code>, <code>focusedItemChanged</code> and <code>itemActivated</code> for\nthese separate actions. <code>itemContextMenu</code> lets the host provide its own menu.\nThe tree exposes ARIA levels, sibling positions, expansion and selection state.</p>\n<p><code>select(item)</code> selects a loaded item without moving browser focus.\n<code>await reveal(item)</code> opens its known ancestors and scrolls to it, also without\nstealing browser focus. It returns false for an unknown item: a remote adapter must\nload its ancestor path first. There is no automatic remote path search.</p>\n<h2 id=\"custom-rows\">Custom rows</h2>\n<p><code>renderItem</code> can populate the row’s content host with an icon, tag and secondary\ntext. Keep content non-interactive: TreeView owns disclosure, keyboard focus and\nselection. Always provide <code>getText</code> for the accessible label and type-ahead.\nThis version uses fixed 30px, single-line rows; custom content must fit that height.</p>\n<p>The <a href=\"?!=/components/html-editor\">HtmlEditor demo</a> also uses TreeView to navigate\nthe editor’s model elements. Structural element selection and the full property\ninspector are separate, later stages.</p>\n",
